[94m[Bash][0m Read jobs implementation $ cat engine/core/src/jobs.cpp
The implementation is mostly sound, but I see two gaps against the "shutdown without accessing destroyed subsystems" criterion:

1. A cancelled pending job keeps its `fn` (and its captures) alive in the record until every `JobHandle` is gone. Captured objects that touch a subsystem would then be destroyed late.
2. `shutdown()` is not safe to call from two threads at once, since both can `join()` the same worker.

I'll check the tests and the CMake labels before changing anything.
