US-006 is verified on every local gate, but not on hosted CI, which has never run this tree. The job system was already in the tree from an earlier pass, so I reviewed it against the acceptance criteria and fixed two shutdown gaps.

**Changes**
- `engine/core/src/jobs.cpp`: a job that reaches a terminal state now drops its task and captures immediately. Before, a cancelled job's captures stayed alive until the last `JobHandle` was released.
- `engine/core/src/jobs.cpp`, `engine/core/include/engine/core/jobs.hpp`: `shutdown()` takes a lifecycle mutex. Two threads calling it at once could both `join()` the same worker.
- `tests/src/core_jobs_tests.cpp`: two new integration tests, one for capture release on cancelled and finished jobs, one for concurrent shutdown.
- `docs/runtime-conventions.md` and `docs/build.md` (verification row) and `.ralph-tui/progress.md` (new entry) are updated.

**Gates on the final tree**
- Linux clang (`ValidateVendor`, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, `linux-unit`): 10/10.
- Linux ASan/UBSan (`linux-asan`, `linux-sanitize`): 10/10.
- Linux GCC 9.4 (`linux-gcc`, `linux-gcc-debug`, `linux-gcc-unit`): 10/10.
- Windows MSVC (`win-gate.bat`: `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, `win-unit`): `WIN_GATES_PASSED`.

**Problems along the way**
- The first Windows run failed on `/WX`: my new test discarded a `[[nodiscard]]` handle. Fixed.
- The first Linux integration run hung. My capture-release test waited on a job while a spinning blocker held the only worker. Fixed by cancelling the blocker first.

